  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>V2U (Vétérinaires 2 Toute Urgence) is a network of on-call clinics dedicated to veterinary emergencies. Its website lists 17, from Paris to Biarritz via Marseille, Nice and Toulon. According to the network's website, the Toulon clinic has handled the region's emergencies since 2012. It is in the west of Toulon, on the N8 national road, at 157 route de Marseille, at the entrance to the city coming from Ollioules, 500 metres after the Polyclinique des Fleurs. It is not a neighbourhood clinic: you come here for an emergency, not for a routine consultation.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The clinic takes over from regular vets outside their hours: it is open 7 days a week, every night from 7pm to 8am the next morning on weekdays, from Saturday noon to Monday 8am, and all day on public holidays. During the day on weekdays it is not open: you then need to go through your usual vet. The website gives 04 27 04 02 70 to reach it, and offers online registration if you want to go straight to the clinic and announce your arrival. Whether you called, registered online or came directly, animals are seen in order of arrival and degree of medical urgency; a veterinary assistant welcomes you, assesses your dog and opens its file.</p>
      <p>As for the team, the website announces two to three emergency vets each evening, one vet present all night to monitor hospitalised animals, and a specialised veterinary assistant (three on Sundays and public holidays during the day). The technical platform includes on-site blood tests, digital radiography, ultrasound, endoscopy, two gas anaesthesia stations with monitoring and intensive-care equipment (oxygen cages, drips). A full surgical suite allows operating on site, for example for a twisted stomach, a chest wound or a swallowed foreign body. A report is sent by email to your usual vet, and hospitalised animals are transferred to them as soon as they open if their condition allows, by you or by an animal transport service.</p>
      <p>The clinic also covers more than 140 veterinary practices in the region, including those of Toulon, La Seyne-sur-Mer, Hyères, Six-Fours-les-Plages, La Garde or Sanary-sur-Mer, under on-call care agreements. The network also has a specialised call centre reachable at any hour on 09 70 24 70 24. The website publishes advice sheets useful to dog owners: heatstroke, viper bite, processionary caterpillars, chocolate poisoning, twisted stomach.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: save 04 27 04 02 70 on your phone and call before heading over to confirm what to do.</div>

      <h2>Worth checking</h2>
      <p>The network's home page shows 04 88 60 20 50 for Toulon, while the clinic's page gives 04 27 04 02 70: if in doubt, try the other number or 09 70 24 70 24.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The clinic is on the edge of the N8 national road, in the west of Toulon. The clinic's page offers route links (Waze, Google Maps, Apple Maps) to find it from your location.</p>
